G1204.def:
δεῦρο 
adv., [in LXX chiefly for לֵךְ, לֵכָה ;] 
__1. of place; 
__(a) hither, with verbs of motion; 
__(b) (in cl. chiefly poët.) as an imperat., here! come!: Matthieu 19:21, Marc 10:21, Luc 18:22, Jean 11:43, Actes 7:3" (LXX) , 34 (LXX), Apocalypse 17:1 21:9. 
__2. Of time, hitherto, now: Apocalypse 1:13.†

G1219.def:
δημόσιος, -α, -ον
(δῆμος), [in LXX: 2Ma.6:10, 3Ma.2:27 4:7 * ;] 
belonging to the people, public: Actes 5:18; dative fem. used adverbially (cl.); 
__(a) at the public expense, by public consent; 
__(b) publicly: Actes 16:37 18:28 20:20.†

G1223.def:
διά (before a vowel δ᾽, exc. Romains 8:10, 2 Corinthiens 5:7, and in (Proper name)s; Tdf., Pr., 94), 
prep. with genitive, accusative, as in cl.; 
__1. with genitive, through; 
__(i) of Place, after verbs of motion or action: Matthieu 2:12 12:43, Marc 2:23, Luc 4:30, Jean 4:4, 2 Corinthiens 11:33, al.; σώζεσθαι (διας-) δ. πυρός, ὕδατος, 1 Corinthiens 3:15, 1 Pierre 3:20; βλέπειν δ. ἐσόπτρου, 1 Corinthiens 13:12; metaphorically, of a state or condition: Romains 14:20, 2 Corinthiens 2:4 5:7, 10; δ. γράμματος, ἀκροβυστίας (Lft., Notes, 263, 279), Romains 2:27 4:11; δι ̓ὑπομενῆς, Romains 8:25. 
__(ii) Of Time; 
__(a) during which: Matthieu 26:61, Marc 14:58, Luc 5:5; δ. παντὸς τοῦ ζῆν, Hébreux 2:15; δ. παντός (διαπαντός in Marc 5:5, Luc 24:53), always, continually, Matthieu 18:10, Actes 2:25" (LXX) 10:2 24:16, Romains 11:10" (LXX), 2 Thessaloniciens 3:16, Hébreux 9:6 13:15. 
__(b) within which: Actes 1:3; δ. νυκτός, Actes 5:19 16:9 17:10 23:31; 
__(with) after which (Field, Notes, 20; Abbott, JG, 255f.): Marc 2:1, Actes 24:17, Galates 2:1. 
__(iii) Of the Means or Instrument; 
__(1) of the efficient cause (regarded also as the instrument): of God, Romains 11:36, 1 Corinthiens 1:9, Galates 4:7, Hébreux 2:10 7:21; of Christ, Romains 1:8 5:1, 17, 1 Corinthiens 15:21, 1 Pierre 4:11, al.; δ. τ. ὑμῶν δεήσεως, Romains 1:12, 2 Corinthiens 1:4, Galates 4:23, al.; 
__(2) of the agent, instrument or means; 
__(a) with genitive of person(s), Matthieu 11:2, Luc 1:70, Jean 1:17, Actes 1:16, Romains 2:16, 1 Corinthiens 1:21, Éphésiens 1:5, Hébreux 2:14, Apocalypse 1:1, al.; ὑπὸ τ. κυρίου δ. τ. προφήτου (δ. τ. κυρίου, 1 Thessaloniciens 4:2 (M, Th., in l.); Lft., Rev., 121f.), Matthieu 1:22 2:15, Romains 1:2; δ. ἐπιστολῆς ὡς δ. ἡμῶν (Field, Notes, 202), 2 Thessaloniciens 2:2; δ. Σ. (NTD, 22), 1 Pierre 5:12; 
__(b) with genitive of thing(s) (where often the simple dative is used in cl.; Jannaris, Gr., 375), Jean 11:4, Actes 5:12; δ. τ. πίστεως, Romains 3:30; δ. λόγου θεοῦ, 1 Pierre 1:23; δ. παραβολῆς, Luc 8:4; δουλεύειν δ. τ. ἀγάπης, Galates 5:13; δ. ἐπαγγελίας, Galates 3:18, 
__2. C. accusative; 
__(i) rarely, as with genitive, through (Hom), δ. μέσον Σαμαρίας (ICC, in l.; Bl., §42, 1; Robertson, Gr., 581), Luc 17:11. 
__(ii) by reason of, because of, for the sake of; 
__(a) with accusative of person(s) (M, Pr., 105), Marc 2:27, Jean 6:57 11:42, Romains 8:20; 
__(b) with accusative of thing(s), δ. φθόνον, Matthieu 27:18, Marc 15:10; δ. φόβον, Jean 7:13 20:19; δ. ἀγάπην, Éphésiens 2:4; δ. τοῦτο, freq., for this cause, therefore, Matthieu 6:25, Marc 6:14, Luc 11:49, Jean 6:65, al.; id. before ὅτι, Jean 5:16 10:17, al.; δ. τί, why, Matthieu 9:11, 14 Marc 2:18, Jean 7:45, al.; δ. τό, with inf., Marc 5:4, Luc 9:7, Jacques 4:2. 
__3. In composition, 
__(1) through, as in διαβαίνω; 
__(2) of separation, asunder, as in διασπάω; 
__(3) of distribution, abroad, as in διαγγέλλω; 
__(4) of transition, as διαλλάσσω; 
__(5) of "perfective" action (M, Pr., 112f., 115f.), as διαφύγω, διακαθαρίζω.

G1224.def:
δια-βαίνω 
[in LXX chiefly for עבר ;] 
__1. to make a stride. 
__2. to step across, cross over; 
__(a) trans.: τ. θάλασσαι, Hébreux 11:29; 
__(b) intrans.: before εἰς, Actes 16:9; πρός, Luc 16:26.†

G1228.def:
διάβολος, -ον
(διαβάλλω, which see) [in LXX for שָׂטָן (as Job 1:6), exc. Esther 7:4 8:1 (צַר, צָרַר) ;] 
slanderous, accusing falsely. As subst., ὁ, ἡ, δ.; 
__(a) generally (of. Es, ll. with), a slanderer, false accuser: 1 Timothée 3:6, 7 (CGT, in l., but see infr.) 3:11, 2 Timothée 3:3, Tite 2:3; 
__(b) as chiefly in LXX, of Satan, the Accuser, the Devil: Matthieu 4:1, 5, 8, 11 13:39 25:41, Luc 4:2, 3, 6, 13 8:12, Jean 13:2, Actes 10:38, Éphésiens 4:27 6:11, 1 Timothée 3:6, 7 (but see supr.), 2 Timothée 2:26, Hébreux 2:14, Jacques 4:7, 1 Pierre 5:8, Ju 9, Apocalypse 2:10 12:9, 12 20:2, 10; εἶναι ἐκ τοῦ δ., Jean 8:44, 1 Jean 3:8; τέκνα τοῦ δ., 1 Jean 3:10; υἱὸς, Actes 13:10; metaphorically, of Judas, Jean 6:70 (Cremer, 121; DCG, ii, 605).†

G1235.def:
δια-γρηγορέω, -ῶ 
__(a) prop., to remain awake (R, mg.); 
__(b) to be fully awake (R, txt.): Luc 9:32.†

G1281.def:
δια-πραγματεύομαι , "perfective compound" (see M, Pr., 118); 
__1. to examine thoroughly (Plat.). 
__2. In late writers (Dion. Hal.), to gain by trading: Luc 19:15.†

G1296.def:
δια-ταγή, -ῆς, ἡ
(διατάσσω), [in LXX: Esther 4:11 (פַּרְשֶׁגֶן)* ;] 
in late writers (Deiss., LAE, 86 ff.) for cl. διάταξις (WH., however, is found in LXX, Psaumes 119:91, al.); 
__(a) disposition (cf. διάταξις for צָבָא; Sm., 4Ki.23:4, Jérémie 8:2 19:13); εἰς διαταγὰς ἀγγέλων, AV, by the disposition of angels (Alf., in l, Field, Notes, 116; but see infr.): Actes 7:53; 
__(b) ordinance (C. I. 3465): Romains 13:2, Actes 7:53, R, txt. (and see mg.; Page and EGT, in l; but also see supr.).†
